## 2. Remote Work Model at BrightPath

### 2.1 Default Model: Hybrid Work

BrightPath operates a **hybrid work model** as the default:

**Bengaluru Headquarters:**
- Employees are expected in the office **minimum 2 days per week** (typically Tuesday and Thursday)
- Three days per week may be worked remotely from home
- Office days may be adjusted for specific team needs or projects
- Flexibility during the summer months (April–May, heat-related considerations)

**Mumbai Sales Office:**
- Sales and account management staff are primarily remote (1–2 office days per week for meetings/customer visits)
- Regional team meetings typically held monthly in-person

**Remote Employees (Approved):**
- Fully remote employees work from home unless there's a team meeting requiring in-person attendance
- Expected to visit the office quarterly or bi-annually for team events or important meetings

### 2.2 Work-From-Home vs. Fully Remote

**Work-From-Home (WFH) Days:**
- Part of the hybrid model (2–3 days per week)
- Employee is working from home but is expected to be available during standard working hours
- Can transition to office on short notice if needed
- Technology and equipment support provided for occasional WFH

**Fully Remote Work:**
- Long-term remote arrangement (indefinite or contracted period)
- Employee is permanently based outside the office
- Requires written approval from VP and signed Remote Work Addendum
- More formal governance and clearer expectations around availability
- Equipment support provided (permanent home office setup)

