## 6. Remote Work Schedule and Office Days

### 6.1 Hybrid Schedule

**Default Schedule for Bengaluru:**

| Day | Location |
|-----|----------|
| Monday | Remote or Flexible |
| Tuesday | Office |
| Wednesday | Remote |
| Thursday | Office |
| Friday | Remote or Flexible |

- Tuesday and Thursday office days are team standards (meetings, collaboration)
- Monday, Wednesday, Friday are typically WFH days, but flexibility exists
- Adjustments can be made by team or individual (with manager approval)

**Flexibility:**
- If an employee prefers different office days (e.g., Monday and Wednesday instead of Tue/Thu), discuss with manager
- If team has alignment that requires Tuesday/Thursday, that supersedes personal preference
- Special circumstances (family needs, commute, health) can be accommodated with manager discussion

### 6.2 Changing Schedule

**Temporary Change:**
- One-off adjustments (e.g., "I need to WFH this Thursday") can be requested same day or day before
- Manager approval typically granted unless there's a business conflict

**Permanent Schedule Change:**
- Request needs to be submitted to manager for approval
- Changes should be minimized (not more than once per quarter)
- If team has standard office days, individual changes may not be accommodated

### 6.3 No-Show or Last-Minute Changes

**Not Showing for Office Day:**
- If an employee is scheduled to be in office but doesn't show without notifying the manager, it's treated as absence
- If due to emergency or health issue, must notify manager immediately
- Repeated unexcused absences on office days may impact performance review

**Last-Minute WFH Request:**
- If an employee usually comes to office but needs to WFH last minute (illness, emergency), they should notify the manager before 9:30 a.m.
- Occasional emergency WFH is understood and accommodated
- Pattern of last-minute changes should be discussed with manager

