## 7. Office Presence Expectations

### 7.1 In-Office Days

**What Employees Should Do on Office Days:**
- Arrive by 9:30 a.m.; check in on HRIS
- Be available for in-person meetings and collaboration
- Participate in team meetings, stand-ups, or planning sessions
- Socialize and build relationships with colleagues (lunch, coffee)
- Engage in mentoring (giving or receiving)
- Participate in company events or celebrations (if held on office days)

**What NOT to Do on Office Days:**
- Come to office just to sit in a corner and work independently (defeats the purpose)
- Attend back-to-back video calls all day (could do this from home)
- Miss meetings or be disengaged
- Leave early without notifying the manager

### 7.2 Fully Remote Office Visit Expectations

For fully remote employees:

**Quarterly Office Visit (Recommended):**
- Spend 3–5 days in the office once per quarter
- Timing can be coordinated around team events or company meetings
- Company covers travel and accommodation costs if employee is in different city

**Semi-Annual Team Offsites:**
- All-hands meetings or company celebrations (typically once or twice per year)
- Remote employees expected to attend in person (travel covered)
- May be virtual option if employee circumstances prevent travel

**Ad-Hoc Office Days:**
- For critical meetings, customer visits, or team collaboration
- Manager may request in-office presence on specific dates
- With 2+ weeks notice, employee should plan to attend

