## 8. Performance Monitoring and Accountability

### 8.1 Performance Expectations

Remote work does NOT mean lower performance expectations:
- Goals and deliverables are the same as office employees
- Quality standards are the same
- Meeting deadlines is critical (even more so when remote, to maintain trust)
- Communication and responsiveness are important

**What Matters:**
- Output and results (did you deliver on goals and deadlines?)
- Responsiveness and communication (are you available and engaged?)
- Collaboration (do you contribute to team projects and discussions?)
- Initiative (are you proactive or reactive?)

**What Doesn't Matter:**
- How many hours you sit at your desk (as long as you deliver 8 hours of work)
- Whether you work 9:00–5:00 or 10:00–6:00 (as long as it's 8 hours)
- Where the work is completed (home or office, as long as it's a secure setup)

### 8.2 Monitoring Remote Work

**Monitoring Methods:**
- Regular 1:1 meetings with manager (weekly)
- Status updates and progress tracking (documented in work system)
- Attendance tracking in HRIS (check-in/check-out)
- Project delivery and milestone tracking
- Peer feedback on collaboration and communication

**What the Company Does NOT Do:**
- Keystroke monitoring or detailed activity tracking
- Automatic screen captures or video monitoring
- Tracking of personal apps or websites
- Requiring constant Slack status updates
- Surprise video call checks on whether you're working

**What the Company MAY Do:**
- Random spot checks of productivity (task completion, deliverables)
- Review of communication and responsiveness patterns
- Audit of system access logs (to detect security issues)
- Review of email and Slack for policy compliance (done rarely, with legal authorization)

### 8.3 If Performance Suffers

If a remote work arrangement is not working:
- Manager will have a conversation: "I've noticed X is slipping. How can we support you?"
- Discussion of whether the issue is related to remote work or another factor
- Options: Increase office days, additional support, performance plan, or end remote arrangement
- Performance issues don't automatically end remote work; issues are addressed directly

