## 12. Leaving Remote Work Arrangement

### 12.1 Employee-Initiated Change

If an employee wants to change from remote to office-based (or vice versa):
- Submit request to manager with reasoning
- Manager reviews; may ask clarifying questions
- If change is feasible (available office space, role supports it), approval is usually given
- Transition period: 2 weeks notice is customary

### 12.2 Company-Initiated Change

The company may require an employee to return to office if:
- Business circumstances change (new office-based project, team expansion)
- Remote work arrangement is not working (performance issues, team collaboration problems)
- Individual role changes significantly
- Security or compliance concerns arise related to remote work

**Notice:**
- Company provides at least 2 weeks notice of change (or 4 weeks for relocations)
- Discussion with employee about the reasons and any accommodations available
- Relocation support may be offered if employee needs to move to be closer to office

